// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: calls through a function pointer
// BUG-1003 (2026-09-06): the BUG-998 hole through the ONE callee form the
// transitive summary cannot resolve — a call through a FUNCTION POINTER. `fp`
// is bound to a function that write-locks S; the statement already holds S's
// write lock. Measured on the pre-fix build: exit 0, the callee's write
// unlocked (EDEADLK ignored) and its unlock releasing the caller's lock.
// Scoped to shared(rw): a plain `shared` root is a recursive mutex, and the
// callback-table idiom (`go.cb();`) must keep compiling.
shared(rw) struct S { u32 v; }
S g;
u32 f() { g.v = 2; return 1; }
u32 main() { *() -> u32 fp = f; g.v = fp(); return 0; }
